  "reasoning": "The patient presents with skin peeling and rashes on the arms, legs, and back, accompanied by joint pain. This combination of dermatological symptoms (peeling, rashes) and musculoskeletal symptoms (joint pain) is highly characteristic of psoriasis, particularly psoriatic arthritis. While other conditions like drug reactions or fungal infections can cause skin rashes, they do not typically present with joint pain. Arthritis accounts for the joint pain but fails to explain the widespread skin peeling and rashes. Therefore, psoriasis is the single diagnosis that comprehensively covers all reported symptoms.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]psoriasis[/DIAGNOSIS]"
